WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.937
This decision guide helps you choose where work belongs.

00:00:02.937 --> 00:00:06.162
Transactional workflows often belong in a database.

00:00:06.162 --> 00:00:09.087
Large file transformations often fit Spark.

00:00:09.087 --> 00:00:12.832
Reusable lakehouse outputs often become Delta tables.

00:00:12.832 --> 00:00:16.867
Small dashboard queries may fit a database or SQL endpoint.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:19.652
Batch feature preparation may fit Spark.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:24.012
The best choice depends on workload, freshness, governance, and scale.

00:00:24.012 --> 00:00:29.372
Connect this idea to a retail pipeline aggregating high-volume sales data across partitions.

00:00:29.372 --> 00:00:33.922
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:33.922 --> 00:00:40.652
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:40.652 --> 00:00:45.167
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:50.000
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
